# seed: 1
# requires: boot_menu hero_ready map_enter path_found hero_move
# Option 7, "Enable automatic Way Point calculations", gates the pathfinder. Its DEFAULT is
# 1 -- it is ON in retail, straight out of the table at DAT_004F2A58 (record 27:
# {7, 1, "Enable automatic Way Point calculations."}), so nothing has to be seeded or ticked
# to run this replay. If a future script needs option 7 OFF, it must go through the Options
# dialog op, because the original has no other way to reach it.
# Evergreen spawn (179,202). The walk view is the map pane, 19,0 325x281 at a 640x480
# client (FUN_0041B891's OnSize, all.c:20906-20961), so the view origin is
# (179-41, 202-35) = (138,167) and one screen pixel is a quarter of a map unit.
# click (149,150) is therefore map (138+32, 167+8) = (170,204): the direct line from the
# snapped start (178,202) hits the shoreline, so FUN_00461DCC detours and the hero walks
# the wall. Observed: path_found nodes=3 x=174 y=206, then hero_move x=170 y=204.
# The node count and order are implementation details of the 10-try wall walk, so this
# asserts only that a path was FOUND and that the hero ARRIVED.
expect boot_menu 900
# FUN_00402A73's Terms of Service modal opens on entry to the main menu (front.c:534
# tos_gate, consumed at front.c:770) and swallows the next key. "I Accept" is
# tos_accept = (356,371,75,23), so its centre is (393,382).
click 393 382
expect tos_accept 300
# State 2 is where FUN_0041F699 makes its synchronous 0x46F call, which raises
# SRNet's modal (0x42AA10). 1005 "Solo Game" is (250,313,299,23) -> centre
# (399,324); control 1 "Play Game" is (250,380,75,23) -> centre (287,391).
# 1005 then 1 closes it, 0x46F returns 1, FUN_0041D374 registers
# "--- Scanning ---", and the stepper FUN_00438E8E runs ~30 calls (6140 to
# 8340 ms) before FUN_0041B891(3) draws the world list.
# Main menu: RETURN is the Play-now shortcut (0x46B) into state 2.
key RETURN
wait 30
click 399 324
wait 10
click 630 309
wait 240
# State 3 is the world list; RETURN takes the highlighted row
# (msg 0x474), which is the keyboard shortcut for the row's click.
key RETURN
wait 30
# Three states before the Well, not two: 1 main menu -> 2 the
# "Where Do You Want To Play Today?" splash (FUN_0041D31F) -> 3 the world
# list (FUN_0041D717). The original's own table is FUN_0041B891 (all.c:21078);
# the port used to collapse the splash, so the script had drifted. The extra
# RETURN is the plan's keyboard shortcut for the row click (msg 0x474).
key n
wait 5
text PathWalker
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
click 149 150
expect path_found 240
expect hero_move 900
quit
